        "id": 1967151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T02:08:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the entries in `tgid_base_stuff` map to `/proc/\u003cpid\u003e/cgroup_v2_freezer_stats` and the ones in `tid_base_stuff` map to `/proc/\u003ctask group leader pid\u003e/task/\u003cpid\u003e/cgroup_v2_freezer_stats`. I have it in `tid_base_stuff` because originally I thought that the long path was the only way to access the counter for a non-group leader task id, but now I\u0027m seeing that you can still read the file at `/proc/\u003cnon leader pid\u003e/cgroup_v2_freezer_stats` even if it doesn\u0027t have an entry when you read `/proc`. My preference is to keep it there in case someone wants to use the `/proc/\u003cgroup leader\u003e/task/...` path to check the freezer time for each subtask, but I\u0027m also happy to remove it if you don\u0027t think anyone would use that!",
      "parentUuid": "05bb39f8_0750a388",
      "revId": "4473005737c4c0039b92cdc18b2611de1162d93f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
